  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "continuously heal all allies; companions deal damage to all enemies",
    "skill1": "attach healing companion to each non-summoned ally, which can bloom into enhanced form",
    "skill2": "heal weakest allies; grant shield if companion is present",
    "skill3": "ATK increased further when companion present",
    "skill4": "companion absorbs excess healing to unlock additional buffs for host",
    "skill5": "companion damage scales on stored excess healing"
  },
  "play_overview": "Solise attaches **healing companions** to each non-summoned ally, then blooms them into **enhanced forms** for extra pressure. Her ultimate **continuously heals all allies** while companions deal **damage to all enemies**. Weakest allies receive direct heals and shields when a companion is present on them. Excess healing is **absorbed by companions** to unlock additional buffs for their hosts. Companion damage **scales on stored excess healing**, turning overheal into offense. She needs **clustered allies and fight time**; spread lines or early burst waste her companion setup.",
  "counter_overview": "Solise attaches **healing companions** at battle start and snowballs **overheal into blooms**, shields, and companion damage — her ultimate **heals the whole team** while companions hit every foe. She is **unaffected while casting**, so do not bank on interrupting Life's Embrace mid-channel. **Lock ally healing** with [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Dunlingr]]'s Curelock (C — pair [[Ravion]] / [[Himmel]]), **delete her early** before blooms with those same picks, and **spread** clustered lines so overheal never charges companions. Add Vitality cuts from [[Frieren]] / [[Gwyneth]] once Curelock is active."
}
